+//! **REVIEWER'S TESTS, token round 16** (independent soundness review; this
+//! file lives only in the reviewer's scratch copy
+//! `ops/zkp-mvp/token-io-review-r16-scratch/`, never in a lane tree).
+//!
+//! * S1 (item 3, D45(2)): which registered policies the R13 Shieldstral
+//!   classifier profiles admit, against the brief's "fixed three-policy list";
+//! * S2 (item 2): every term of the R13 whole-run figure printed for the
+//!   reviewer's independent recompute (`r16/bits_r16.py`), the exact floors
+//!   per policy, and `--min-bits` enforced at both profiles (95 passes the
+//!   floor door, one more is refused);
+//! * S3 (item 7): a cheating prover with a WRONG activation set (the role of
+//!   the CLI's `--seq-dir`) cannot make an accepting receipt for the sealed
+//!   input — three ways, on native R13's h24 rung with two gate denominators;
+//! * S4 (item 4): the N-r13-5 reuse refuses a derivation without a row or of
+//!   the wrong width, and never streams again when it has the row.
